{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfS7xf8dwzaGCwsLThRZe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a complete understanding of the architecture. Let me summarize my findings:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- `Shipment.kt:9-27` — Entity with `status: ShipmentStatus` enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- `ShipmentController.kt:20-56` — Controller using POST for create, GET for read, no state transitions yet\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt:15-18` — Repository with `save()` method for persistence (read-modify-write pattern)\n- `ApiExceptions.kt:18-24` — Exception types: `ResourceNotFoundException` (404) and `ConflictException` (409)\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` — `ErrorCode` enum (currently: ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED)\n- `ShipmentControllerTest.kt:1-84` — Existing tests using MockMvc with `post()` and `jsonPath()`\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n1. Errors thrown as `ApiException` subclasses, handled centrally by `GlobalExceptionHandler`\n2. Each error state maps to specific `ErrorCode` enum value\n3. Controllers return `ResponseEntity<T>` with status codes\n4. Repository pattern: inject repository, call `save()`, `findById()`, `existsById()`\n5. Tests use MockMvc with `post()`, `jsonPath()`, and status matchers\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` — Add `POST /{shipmentId}/confirm` method\n2. `ApiError.kt` — Add `ErrorCode` for rejected state transitions (needed for CANCELLED rejection)\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Add 4 tests: confirm created, confirm already confirmed, reject cancelled, reject unknown id\n\n**Risks:**\n- The repository's `save()` is used for both creates and updates; read-modify-write in `confirm()` is not atomic under concurrent access\n- Error code naming convention: should follow existing pattern (SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED or similar)\n\n**Open questions:** None — requirements are explicit.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **`ApiError.kt`** — Add `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED` to the `ErrorCode` enum. This is the only way to satisfy the 409 response for CANCELLED shipments while following the error contract.\n\n2. **`ShipmentController.kt`** — Add method:\n   ```kotlin\n   @PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")\n   fun confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): Shipment {\n       val shipment = repository.findById(shipmentId)\n           ?: throw ResourceNotFoundException(...)\n       \n       if (shipment.status == ShipmentStatus.CANCELLED) {\n           throw ConflictException(ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED, \"Shipment is cancelled\")\n       }\n       \n       if (shipment.status == ShipmentStatus.CONFIRMED) {\n           return shipment  // Idempotent: already confirmed, return as-is\n       }\n       \n       val confirmed = shipment.copy(status = ShipmentStatus.CONFIRMED)\n       return repository.save(confirmed)\n   }\n   ```\n\n3. **`ShipmentControllerTest.kt`** — Add 4 tests:\n   - **`confirms a created shipment and persists it`** — POST to `/shipments/S-1/confirm` returns 200 with status=CONFIRMED\n   - **`confirm is idempotent on already confirmed shipments`** — POST twice to same endpoint, second returns 200 with no change\n   - **`rejects confirming a cancelled shipment`** — Insert CANCELLED shipment directly to repo, POST confirm returns 409 with SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED code\n   - **`rejects confirming a non-existent shipment`** — POST confirm to unknown ID returns 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Use existing error codes (e.g., VALIDATION_FAILED) for the CANCELLED case: Rejected because it's semantically wrong. The error is not validation; it's a state conflict. Adding a specific error code follows the pattern established by SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Read | Write | Response | Mechanism |\n|------|-------|------|-------|----------|-----------|\n| CREATED → CONFIRMED | POST `/shipments/S-1/confirm` | `repository.findById(S-1)` returns Shipment(status=CREATED) | `repository.save(copy with CONFIRMED)` | 200 + Shipment JSON | Controller returns entity |\n| Already CONFIRMED (retry) | POST `/shipments/S-1/confirm` | `findById(S-1)` returns Shipment(status=CONFIRMED) | None (already correct) | 200 + Shipment JSON | Early return in controller |\n| CANCELLED (conflict) | POST `/shipments/S-1/confirm` | `findById(S-1)` returns Shipment(status=CANCELLED) | None | 409 + ApiError | `throw ConflictException(SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED)` |\n| Unknown ID | POST `/shipments/S-missing/confirm` | `findById(S-missing)` returns null | None | 404 + ApiError | `throw ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND)` |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **confirm_created_shipment** — Test the happy path: POST creates, POST confirm moves to CONFIRMED, GET verifies persistence\n2. **confirm_is_idempotent** — Test retry safety: POST confirm twice, both succeed with 200 and same result\n3. **confirm_rejects_cancelled** — Test state validation: Insert CANCELLED directly to repo, POST confirm returns 409 with correct error code\n4. **confirm_rejects_unknown_id** — Test not found case: POST confirm to non-existent ID returns 404 with correct error code\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the design:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2586,"cache_read_input_tokens":19174,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2586},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4a8fed83-ef57-4b0f-a039-7e9b00f95f8d","uuid":"ba0a80a3-eae4-4281-b1ac-7fe1e5286232","timestamp":"2026-09-26T13:21:50.189